{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "064cece0-d180-4cff-bcb1-a1415895a694",
    "name": "Chat Backend",
    "description": "Chat against real LOS dev logins, one folder per person. The numbered requests are the sign-in flow, run by hand in order; each saves the token the next step needs, and a failed step clears the tokens after it.\n\nCustomer: 1. LOS login → 2. Chat session → chat requests (Bearer {{customerToken}}).\nStaff: 1. LOS login → 2. LOS handoff → 3. Chat session → chat requests (Bearer {{staffToken}}).\n\nEach chat session step also saves a refresh token (customerRefreshToken / staffRefreshToken); \"Refresh chat session\" renews the chat token without signing in again, \"Log out\" ends the login.\n\nOnly the chat session tokens (customerToken, staffToken) work on chat requests. Leave the chat requests' Authorization on \"Inherit auth from parent\".",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "36185983"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Customer",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. LOS login (LOS checks the password)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "let body; try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 && body && body.data) {",
                  "  const d = body.data;",
                  "  pm.environment.set('losCustomerToken', d.accessToken);",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('losCustomerToken');",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('customerToken');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('response is JSON (if not, losUrl/baseUrl points at the wrong host)', () => pm.expect(body).to.be.an('object'));",
                  "if (pm.response.code !== 200 && body) pm.test('reason: ' + JSON.stringify(body.error || body.message || body), () => { throw new Error('see test name'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{customerUsername}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{customerPin}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{losUrl}}/customer/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{losUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "customer",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Logs in on LOS dev. Saves losCustomerToken: an LOS token, only used by step 2."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Chat session (swap the LOS token for a chat token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "let body; try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201 && body && body.data) {",
                  "  const d = body.data;",
                  "  pm.environment.set('customerToken', d.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.environment.set('customerRefreshToken', d.refreshToken);",
                  "  console.log('customer chat session for', d.user.username, '- valid', d.expiresIn);",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('customerToken');",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('customerRefreshToken');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('response is JSON (if not, losUrl/baseUrl points at the wrong host)', () => pm.expect(body).to.be.an('object'));",
                  "if (pm.response.code !== 201 && body) pm.test('reason: ' + JSON.stringify(body.error || body.message || body), () => { throw new Error('see test name'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"losToken\": \"{{losCustomerToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/customer/api/v1/auth/session",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "customer",
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "session"
              ]
            },
            "description": "chat_backend checks the LOS signature, finds or creates the chat account, and returns its own session. Saves customerToken (1 h), used by every chat request below. Also saves customerRefreshToken (until refreshExpiresAt, 24 h), used by Refresh and Log out."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh chat session (rotates the refresh token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "let body; try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 && body && body.data) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('customerToken', body.data.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.environment.set('customerRefreshToken', body.data.refreshToken);",
                  "  console.log('refreshed; login ends at', body.data.refreshExpiresAt);",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('customerToken');",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('customerRefreshToken');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "if (pm.response.code !== 200 && body) pm.test('reason: ' + JSON.stringify(body.error || body), () => { throw new Error('see test name'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{customerRefreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/customer/api/v1/auth/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "customer",
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                [
                  "refresh"
                ]
              ]
            },
            "description": "Swaps customerRefreshToken for a new customerToken and a new customerRefreshToken; the old refresh token stops working. Sending an old one again ends the whole login (401), so after a 401 run the sign-in steps again."
          },
          "response": []
        },
